<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johannes Gutenberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1400–<a href="/years/1468">1468</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Gutenberg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Johannes Gutenberg was a fifteenth-century German craftsman who developed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> with movable metal type in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. His press transformed the spread of knowledge in Europe. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bi-sheng">Bi Sheng</a> had invented <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/movable-type">movable type</a> around 1040 CE under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a>, about four centuries earlier.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johannes-gutenberg.jpg" alt="Johannes Gutenberg" width="315" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kenneth C. Zirkel · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mainz_Gutenbergdenkmal_2016_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Printing, pioneered by <b>Johannes Gutenberg</b> at Mainz around 1450, together with German scholarship and craft traditions flourishing in the commercially active free cities, spread innovation across Europe more effectively than any centralised cultural programme could have achieved.</blockquote><a href="/empire/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>Bi Sheng invented movable type using ceramic characters around 1040, some four centuries before <b>Gutenberg</b>'s printing press.</blockquote><a href="/empire/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty · At a glance</a></li><li><blockquote>Printing with movable metal type, developed by <b>Johannes Gutenberg</b> at Mainz around 1450, made books and pamphlets cheap and quick to produce.</blockquote><a href="/movement/protestant-reformation">Protestant Reformation · Background</a></li><li><blockquote>Paper was made at Fangmatan in the 2nd century BCE; woodblock printing appears in China before 220 CE, on silk; movable type followed about 1040, and the printing press of <b>Johannes Gutenberg</b> at Mainz about 1440.</blockquote><a href="/essays/who-invented-it-first">Who Invented It First?</a></li><li><blockquote>The rubricator and binder Henricus Cremer finished his work on a copy of the <b>Gutenberg</b> Bible, the earliest dated copy known.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/august-24">24 August in history</a></li><li><blockquote>By tradition, <b>Johannes Gutenberg</b>'s Bible was completed in Mainz around this date.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/february-23">23 February in history</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=50,8.27&amp;year=1444" aria-label="Mainz on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4740 424 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Johannes Gutenberg"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5190 694h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5190 694h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=50,8.27&amp;year=1444">What was here in 1444? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
